---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="/uses :: Jesse Wunderlich"
  description="The hardware, software, and tools Jesse Wunderlich uses to build."
  ogTitle="What Jesse uses">
  <div class="box">
    <h2>&gt; /uses</h2>
    <p class="lead">The gear and tools I actually reach for. (A
    <a href="https://uses.tech" rel="noopener">/uses page</a> — the running list of what's in
    my kit.)</p>

    <div class="uses-cat">
      <h3>// hardware</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Apple ecosystem — iPhone + Mac</li>
        <li class="todo">TODO: which Mac, monitor, keyboard, desk setup?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-cat">
      <h3>// dev</h3>
      <ul>
        <li class="todo">TODO: editor (VS Code? Cursor?), terminal, shell</li>
        <li>Stack I build on: Next.js / Astro / TypeScript / Tailwind</li>
        <li>Hosting: Vercel · DNS: Cloudflare</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-cat">
      <h3>// the AI sidekick</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Yishai — my OpenClaw assistant who helps me build (including this site)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="uses-cat">
      <h3>// day job</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>ScanEagle UAS — what I fly for Insitu / Boeing</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size:.75rem;color:#666;">This list is a work in progress — Jesse to fill the TODOs.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
